      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a9b3ad0f5e0532e3ea468be|full_name}: I appreciate your analogy, as real-world regulations requiring accessibility for businesses and public spaces are a real social good.\nI don't think the analogy applies here. What we're talking about here is a default where the world has the accessibility already. Creators would need to spend energy and resources to remove it. In the real world the situation is the opposite.\nI very much do not think systemic neglect or abuse would result from this. The vast majority of VRChat worlds will remain safe and accessible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
