      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This canny just seems like they are just thinking about themselves and not the people that may need it. It feels like big \"my things are important\" creator complex. Cant you just use a sign or something saying to turn off earmuff mode? The same way you do when the volume has to be set to a certain %.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62f134d8633a3a44d1eb2274",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5a9de400f3791b4155afcc5b",
        "alias": "Rosé pink Yak",
        "aliasID": "65c27b10ed6eefce4c7d7976",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/741d2a4dc4373e8d9e2a33764535be3b.png",
        "created": "2018-03-06T00:42:40.626Z",
        "name": "FairlySadPanda",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-08-08T16:07:52.418Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62ee519b380aa644b3b0fab1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Seen a lot of back-and-forth on this request both here and elsewhere so I'm going to try and give a clear example of the problem, and why implementing the request is way better for everyone.\nTo be clear before I begin:\n0. Earmuffs is a great feature!\n1. World creators should not make bad worlds and will need to consider earmuff users going forwards!\nBy far the most important use of Udon audio overrides at the moment is for PA systems, where a speaker or speakers are on stage and there's some way to amplify the speaker's voice, usually via a range boost (and a gain decrease to make sure the range does not blow people's ears out).\nA great use of earmuffs is to attend an event in a crowded instance, listen to some cool music and hang out with friends. Let's assume Alice joins an instance to hang out with her friend Barry, with Charity, the world creator, running the event. Alice doesn't like lots of chatter around her in VRC, so she sets her earmuffs setting to 2m, with an exterior audio of 0%. She wants to enjoy the club and talk to Barry, and maybe some other people in a conversation bubble, but otherwise hear the music clearly.\nAt the top of the hour, Charity uses the world's PA system to announce that the event is going to continue in a new instance, and folks need to take the portal to said instance. \nAlice, because her exterior audio is at 0%, does not hear Charity. In fact, she can't hear any PA information - and depending on the event, that PA information could be important stuff (\"don't run on stage\", \"use a performant avatar\", \"the DJ's computer just caught fire, she'll be back in a few minutes\", etc).\nWhat's Alice supposed to do here? She can't both have her earmuff settings how she likes them and hear the PA system. She has to turn up the exterior audio in case there is a PA announcement.\nWhat's Charity supposed to do? There's no Udon hooks to detect earmuff mode being on or off, so she doesn't have a good way of knowing if her PA system is going to be audible by everyone. She has to implement a more complex alternate system, or have to manage earmuff users at events to make sure they heard important announcements, which takes time away from other event management duties.\nTo me, the obvious solution given infinite time and no technical restraints would be a system similar to the near culling distance settings:\n1. Earmuffs off\n2. Earmuffs on, but Udon can override if needed\n3. Earmuffs forced on with a warning that this might cause issues if the world was built with Udon player audio overrides.\nThis gives Alice total authority over their experience, and reduces Charity to only having to worry about \"forced on\" earmuff users, who are probably using the system for really important comfort reasons which ultimately trump a PA system or similar (rather than just because earmuff mode is just flatly superior to regular VRChat player audio settings).\nThis would break the feature out into a comfort setting (Earmuffs on) and an accessibility setting (Earmuffs forced on), and I think that makes the most logical and user-oriented feature.\nIf the above would take too long to implement, I think it is for the best to allow world creators to make sure people should or should not be heard as neccessary, and stick to the current VRChat ethos of \"if the world sucks, people won't use it.\" If a world creator messes with player audio and makes it intolerable for people even with earmuffs on, then that world creator should get polite but firm feedback from users.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
